  "notes": "Require a compatible cooler-current calibration before making a hardware verdict.\n\nThe archived cooler reference was measured at PWM 180; extrapolating that single point to PWM 255 produced an unsupported low-current conclusion. Runtime cooler comparisons now require a reference at the measured duty (within half an 8-bit step). Other component scaling is unchanged. Unmatched fan expectations also keep aggregate/mixed-load inference inconclusive.\n\nA qualified cooler acquisition without a compatible reference retains actual current, count and time as Unknown/NoReference, without creating or clearing a hardware fault. The supervisor reports ReferenceUnavailable and stops repeating pulses for that missing calibration. Isolated no-load proof, independent overcurrent cutoff and confirmed fault protection remain. No threshold was widened and no suspect measurement was learned as healthy.\n\nConnected-device validation retained eight cooler samples, 690.532 mA mean, valid LEDC route at 996 ms, no cooler-current latch and no repeat for the unavailable reference. This is not a fan-health PASS. Heater acquisition completed; all 64 learned flashlight rows remain unchanged. Primary IR/NTC faults and an intermittent CRT address-safety startup deferral remain under investigation; no complete QA success is claimed.\n\nValidation: fresh independent reviews, 43 host suites, checked ESP32-S3 build, actual ELF/map deadline audit, exact USB END/hash and normal Desktop/Twin readback. Static RAM is unchanged. Firmware: 3166096 bytes; SHA-256 ae2599328a3de8f5090759353c965cd1f9473e91cebf9405cfdd785051a9e45e.\n",
